  OPEN        : Pod and container state from Kubernetes events: were the newly created workloads ever Running and Ready, or stuck pulling images, pending scheduling, or crash-looping before writing a first log line? No dispatch queried the orchestrator.
  OPEN        : Latency and saturation were never measured for any of the four services; only the error-ratio template was run [tr_6a0a1142c89c, tr_73654c07a93e], so a slow-dependency or resource-pressure mechanism remains untested.
  OPEN        : What actually triggered the critical alert at 16:06:34 and which signal it fired on — no evidence on the board reproduces an alertable condition.
  OPEN        : Whether the three unmeasured edges crossed by triage hide a backend (post-storage, Redis/Mongo, or a service-discovery layer) that was never dispatched against.

